 "doc": "The MUFU tables (verity.ml.circuits.ops.mufu) as the special-function unit's piecewise quadratic interpolation, exact: the word at index i is base + ((C0[g] + C1[g] u + (C2[g] Q) << square_shift) >> shift), g = i >> offset_bits the segment, u the offset below it, and Q the hardware's truncated square: of u^2's folded partial products, u_a at 2^(2a) and u_a u_b (a < b) at 2^(a+b+1), the sum of those at or above 2^square_from, shifted right by square_from. Every word but rsq's first (1/sqrt(1) = 1.0, one above the interpolant) is the interpolant. Coefficients found per segment from the measured words: C1, C2 by least squares, then the integers near them for which some C0 puts every word of the segment in [C0 + ..., C0 + ... + 2^shift); each segment has exactly one such (C1, C2) and C0 is the least.",
